  "prompt": "A parabola in the xy-plane has vertex\n[Figure 1]\nand passes through the point\n[Figure 2]\n. The equation of this parabola can be written in the form\n[Figure 3]\n, where\n[Figure 4]\nis a constant. What is the value of\n[Figure 5]\n?",
  "choices": {
    "A": "[Figure 6]",
    "B": "[Figure 7]",
    "C": "[Figure 8]",
    "D": "[Figure 9]"
  },
  "correctAnswer": "B",
  "explanation": "Since the parabola passes through $(9, 16)$ and has the form $y = a(x-7)^2 + 4$, substitute $x=9$ and $y=16$: $16 = a(9-7)^2 + 4$. This simplifies to $16 = 4a + 4$, so $12 = 4a$, giving $a = 3$.\n\nWhy D is incorrect:\n\nThis results from forgetting to square the difference in the vertex form, treating the equation as $16 = a(9-7) + 4$ instead of $16 = a(9-7)^2 + 4$.",
